From 092d8a0be2dc3de543bb77077533c596ed741b7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EssenMoon <yueqrgg@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:08:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] doc: warn that the old pop-up plugs do not exist on current
 Vim

<plug>(MUcompleteCR) and friends are only defined for Vim 8.0.0282 and
older.  An expression mapping that returns one of them on Vim 8.0.0283
or later inserts the plug name as literal text.  Make that explicit in
the plug list and point to the supported <cr> mapping in mucomplete-tips.
---
 doc/mucomplete.txt | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/mucomplete.txt b/doc/mucomplete.txt
index d6b195c..b06bdde 100644
--- a/doc/mucomplete.txt
+++ b/doc/mucomplete.txt
@@ -417,7 +417,11 @@ The following mappings are defined only in Vim 8.0.0282 or older.
 	<plug>(MUcompleteCycFwd) and <plug>(MUcompleteCycBwd) are remapped by
 	the user. See |mucomplete-mappings| for an example.
 
-The following plugs are defined only in Vim 8.0.0282 or older.
+The following plugs are defined only in Vim 8.0.0282 or older.  They do
+not exist in Vim 8.0.0283 and later, so an expression mapping that
+returns one of them on a current Vim inserts the plug name as literal
+text.  On Vim 8.0.0283 and later, map <cr> as shown in
+|mucomplete-tips| instead.
 
 <plug>(MUcompletePopupCancel)
 <plug>(MUcompletePopupAccept)
-- 
2.55.0

